From 6d2ae55c4d1d5fa9ff3338edc0c382a97833198a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opt <a@b>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:17:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(threading): lock-free parallel_for pool with bounded
 spin before sleeping

Iterations are claimed by CAS on a packed (generation, next-iteration) word instead of under the pool mutex, and idle
workers / the waiting caller busy-wait for up to 100us before blocking on a condition variable. Chonk proving issues
~5000 parallel_for calls per proof, roughly half of them shorter than 50us, and waking blocked workers cost ~25us per
call on average.

Adds a stress test of many back-to-back parallel_for calls of varying size.
